# Adamantan-1-ol + 10 MeOH: XTB2 MD, spherical confinement
# FIXED: two problems in the original file.
#   1) The MeOH block was truncated mid-copy: only 59 of the expected 60
#      solvent atoms were present (the first MeOH molecule was missing its
#      hydroxyl H). Total declared atoms = 86 (should be 87), giving an ODD
#      electron count for a singlet - almost certainly the "atom count"
#      error reported earlier.
#   2) Even with the missing H added back, the Apixaban-scale placement
#      (offset 12.78 Ang, sphere radius 14.0 centered at Apixaban's old
#      centroid) put 9 atoms outside the confinement sphere for this much
#      smaller solute (Adamantanol max atom-centroid distance = 3.27 Ang vs
#      Apixaban's 9.03 Ang).
#
# This version:
#   - Restores the complete 10 MeOH molecules (60 atoms), reusing the same
#     well-formed internal MeOH geometry used elsewhere in this project,
#     rigidly translated (orientation preserved) to new anchor points around
#     Adamantanol.
#   - Sphere/placement center = Adamantanol's own centroid for this geometry
#     (29.797, -20.187, -0.371).
#   - 10 MeOH molecules placed (by their own centroid) at offset 6.5 Ang from
#     that centroid, along the same 12 directions used throughout this
#     project.
#   - Cell Sphere radius reduced to 10.0 Ang (vs the old 14.0).
# Checked: min MeOH-Adamantanol atom distance = 2.90 Ang (no clash), max atom
#   distance from the sphere center = 7.92 Ang (safely inside the 10.0 Ang
#   sphere). Total atom count = 87 (27 + 10x6), verified.

! XTB2 MD

%md
  Timestep 1.0_fs
  Initvel 298.15_K
  Thermostat NHC 298.15_K Timecon 20.0_fs
  Cell Sphere 29.797, -20.187, -0.371, 10.0 Spring 20
  Dump Position Stride 100 Filename "Adamantanol_10MeOH_XTB.xyz"
  Run 20000
end

